53
00:03:36,250 --> 00:03:38,500
You're taking a class? That's so cool.

54
00:03:38,840 --> 00:03:41,840
I really liked that Lamaze class I took.

55
00:03:42,090 --> 00:03:45,800
I thought this time I'd go for something more intellectual...

56
00:03:46,050 --> 00:03:48,390
...with a less painful final exam.

57
00:03:49,770 --> 00:03:51,310
That sounds like fun.

58
00:03:51,600 --> 00:03:53,770
Oh, you should come with me!

59
00:03:54,020 --> 00:03:56,230
Then I'll have someone to sit with.

60
00:03:56,400 --> 00:03:57,440
Okay.

61
00:03:57,610 --> 00:04:00,320
Yay! Okay. Ooh, but, do you have time to read it?

62
00:04:00,490 --> 00:04:01,570
I read it in school.

63
00:04:01,740 --> 00:04:05,700
This is going to be so much fun! Shh. I have to finish.

64
00:04:09,950 --> 00:04:10,990
Hi.

65
00:04:12,410 --> 00:04:13,500
What's wrong, buddy?

66
00:04:13,670 --> 00:04:16,040
Someone at work ate my sandwich.

67
00:04:18,040 --> 00:04:20,090
What did the police say?

68
00:04:21,090 --> 00:04:24,050
My Thanksgiving leftover sandwich.

69
00:04:24,300 --> 00:04:26,130
I can't believe someone ate it.

70
00:04:26,390 --> 00:04:27,640
It's just a sandwich.

71
00:04:27,890 --> 00:04:29,470
Just a sandwich?

72
00:04:29,720 --> 00:04:31,640
I am 30 years old, okay?

73
00:04:31,890 --> 00:04:34,180
I'll be divorced twice and I got evicted.

74
00:04:34,440 --> 00:04:37,690
That sandwich was the only good thing in my life!

75
00:04:37,900 --> 00:04:41,690
Someone ate the only good thing going on in my life!

76
00:04:43,700 --> 00:04:46,030
I have enough for one more sandwich.

77
00:04:46,240 --> 00:04:48,780
I was going to eat it myself, but...

78
00:04:50,240 --> 00:04:53,950
Mon, that would be incredible. Thank you so much.

79
00:04:54,410 --> 00:04:57,170
I still can't believe someone ate it!

80
00:04:59,340 --> 00:05:01,550
Look, I left a note and everything.

81
00:05:02,800 --> 00:05:04,210
"Knock-knock." "Who's there?"

82
00:05:04,470 --> 00:05:06,260
"Ross Geller's lunch."

83
00:05:07,180 --> 00:05:09,220
"Ross Geller's lunch, who?"

84
00:05:09,550 --> 00:05:13,310
"Ross Geller's lunch. Please don't take me. Okay?"

85
00:05:14,980 --> 00:05:17,270
I'm surprised you didn't wear it home. Ha-ha-ha.

86
00:05:19,060 --> 00:05:21,770
Want to keep your food? Scare people off.

87
00:05:21,980 --> 00:05:23,570
I learned that on the street.

88
00:05:23,740 --> 00:05:24,780
Really?

89
00:05:25,490 --> 00:05:27,320
What would you say, Pheebs?

90
00:05:27,530 --> 00:05:31,620
Stuff like, uh, "Keep your mitts off my grub."

91
00:05:33,240 --> 00:05:37,710
Do you picture Phoebe on the street with the entire cast of Annie?

92
00:05:40,340 --> 00:05:43,210
This'll keep them away from your stuff.

93
00:05:46,380 --> 00:05:48,050
Whoa!

94
00:05:49,720 --> 00:05:51,680
Phoebe, you are a badass!

95
00:05:53,220 --> 00:05:55,850
Someday I'll tell you how I stabbed the cop.

96
00:05:56,020 --> 00:05:58,520
Phoebe.

97
00:05:56,020 --> 00:05:58,520
He stabbed me first!

98
00:06:02,610 --> 00:06:05,940
The Bronte sisters were remarkable women for their time.

99
00:06:06,190 --> 00:06:08,530
They lived in a patriarchal society.

100
00:06:08,780 --> 00:06:10,660
Sorry I'm late, but I left late.

101
00:06:11,240 --> 00:06:13,030
Ahem.

102
00:06:11,240 --> 00:06:13,030
Okay.

103
00:06:13,740 --> 00:06:16,290
So, what is the book about?

104
00:06:16,540 --> 00:06:18,290
Didn't you read it in high school?

105
00:06:18,500 --> 00:06:21,540
I started it, but then there was this pep rally.

106
00:06:21,750 --> 00:06:23,540
And I was on top of the pyramid.

107
00:06:24,090 --> 00:06:25,550
But anyway, um...

108
00:06:25,760 --> 00:06:26,800
...what's the book about?

109
00:06:28,050 --> 00:06:31,760
It's a tragic love story between Cathy and Heathcliff.

110
00:06:32,010 --> 00:06:34,890
It takes place on these creepy moors in England.

111
00:06:35,140 --> 00:06:39,230
Which I think represent the wildness of Heathcliff's character.

112
00:06:39,480 --> 00:06:41,140
I totally get symbolism.

113
00:06:42,770 --> 00:06:45,320
How would you characterize the theme of this book?

114
00:06:45,480 --> 00:06:47,900
Uh, let's see... Rachel Green?

115
00:06:51,740 --> 00:06:53,280
Ahem, um...

116
00:06:53,450 --> 00:06:57,290
I would have to say that it's a tragic love story.

117
00:06:57,910 --> 00:07:00,250
That's sort of a given...

118
00:07:00,460 --> 00:07:02,420
...but, yes. Anyone else?

119
00:07:03,040 --> 00:07:04,750
Oh, oh, oh. Symbolism!

120
00:07:07,800 --> 00:07:10,170
And the wildness of the moors...

121
00:07:10,430 --> 00:07:12,880
...which I think, is mirrored...

122
00:07:13,140 --> 00:07:16,560
...in the wildness of, uh, Heathcliff's character.

123
00:07:18,060 --> 00:07:21,640
Excellent! What Rachel has shrewdly observed here...

124
00:07:23,100 --> 00:07:24,980
You completely stole my answer!

125
00:07:25,230 --> 00:07:26,980
Honey, that was pretty obvious.

126
00:07:27,230 --> 00:07:29,480
How would you know? You didn't read it!

127
00:07:31,490 --> 00:07:34,910
What do you think? Uh, you in the blue shirt?

128
00:07:37,540 --> 00:07:42,210
I think that, um, yours is a question with many possible answers.

129
00:07:43,580 --> 00:07:48,380
Would you care to venture one?

130
00:07:50,050 --> 00:07:54,510
Are you just repeating me?

131
00:07:56,720 --> 00:07:58,350
All right. Let's move on.

132
00:07:59,270 --> 00:08:00,310
Okay, then.

133
00:08:04,480 --> 00:08:06,860
Why didn't you say you hadn't read the book?

134
00:08:07,110 --> 00:08:09,570
I didn't want him to think I was stupid.

135
00:08:09,820 --> 00:08:12,900
That was really embarrassing, what happened to you.

136
00:08:15,070 --> 00:08:17,070
Phoebe! Phoebe!

137
00:08:15,070 --> 00:08:17,070
Yeah?

138
00:08:17,580 --> 00:08:18,830
Your note?

139
00:08:19,240 --> 00:08:20,290
Amazing!

140
00:08:20,830 --> 00:08:23,160
Not only did no one touch my sandwich...

141
00:08:23,410 --> 00:08:26,210
...but people at work are actually afraid of me.

142
00:08:26,750 --> 00:08:28,460
A guy called me "Mental."

143
00:08:28,710 --> 00:08:30,130
"Mental Geller."

144
00:08:30,710 --> 00:08:33,470
I've always wanted a cool nickname like that.

145
00:08:34,840 --> 00:08:38,390
The best you got in high school was, uh, "Wet Pants Geller."

146
00:08:38,640 --> 00:08:40,390
It was the water fountain, okay?

147
00:08:42,520 --> 00:08:43,600
Anyway...

148
00:08:45,310 --> 00:08:47,150
...people are writing reports for me...

149
00:08:47,310 --> 00:08:50,070
...uh, pushing back deadlines to fit my schedule.

150
00:08:50,320 --> 00:08:52,530
I tell you, you get tough with people...

151
00:08:52,740 --> 00:08:55,530
...and you can get anything you want.

152
00:08:55,740 --> 00:08:58,740
Hey, Tribbiani! Give me that coffee! Now!

153
00:09:08,580 --> 00:09:10,170
This was really fun.

154
00:09:11,670 --> 00:09:13,590
I've been wondering if you'd ask me out.

155
00:09:13,840 --> 00:09:16,170
So you, uh, still wondering?

156
00:09:17,090 --> 00:09:19,260
No. We just went out.

157
00:09:22,390 --> 00:09:23,430
You're smart.

158
00:09:23,680 --> 00:09:25,520
I like that.

159
00:09:27,230 --> 00:09:28,440
Oh.

160
00:09:32,610 --> 00:09:34,280
Oh, candles!

161
00:09:36,360 --> 00:09:37,950
What is that, a blanket?

162
00:09:38,200 --> 00:09:40,660
A video camera? Oh, my God!

163
00:09:40,830 --> 00:09:42,030
No, no, no. Wait.

164
00:09:42,200 --> 00:09:47,330
I can't believe you thought you'd tape us having sex on the first date!

165
00:09:52,300 --> 00:09:53,340
Hi.

166
00:09:55,300 --> 00:09:57,470
Joey, is what she just said, um...

167
00:09:58,720 --> 00:09:59,970
Oh, my God!

168
00:10:00,220 --> 00:10:01,680
You're actually going...

169
00:10:06,560 --> 00:10:08,100
What is going on here?

170
00:10:10,770 --> 00:10:14,020
And with Chandler in the next room. What are you, sick?

171
00:10:19,360 --> 00:10:20,780
I'm Joey.

172
00:10:23,830 --> 00:10:25,660
I mean, I'm disgusting.

173
00:10:28,290 --> 00:10:30,540
I make low-budget adult films.

174
00:10:35,500 --> 00:10:37,050
Huh.

175
00:10:40,970 --> 00:10:42,970
You promised to be more careful!

176
00:10:43,220 --> 00:10:46,310
The good Joey name's been dragged through the mud!

177
00:10:48,520 --> 00:10:49,560
We're so sorry.

178
00:10:49,810 --> 00:10:51,270
I'm telling everyone.

179
00:10:51,480 --> 00:10:56,270
It's the only explanation that doesn't make me look like a pig!

180
00:10:56,650 --> 00:10:58,320
No, there's a better explanation.

181
00:10:58,570 --> 00:11:02,070
Tell them you had to make an adult film for your...

182
00:11:02,280 --> 00:11:04,530
...adult film class.

183
00:11:05,830 --> 00:11:07,450
I like that. But no!

184
00:11:07,700 --> 00:11:11,000
How does that explain my underwear at your place?

185
00:11:12,540 --> 00:11:13,670
I don't know.

186
00:11:14,540 --> 00:11:17,460
Get ready to come out of the non-gay closet.

187
00:11:18,340 --> 00:11:21,760
I promise to come up with something. Just give us time.

188
00:11:23,140 --> 00:11:24,180
All right.

189
00:11:24,930 --> 00:11:27,510
But it better make me look really good.

190
00:11:28,890 --> 00:11:30,230
And another thing...

191
00:11:30,690 --> 00:11:32,060
The video camera?

192
00:11:32,310 --> 00:11:33,560
Nice!

193
00:11:41,570 --> 00:11:42,700
Ross?

194
00:11:43,280 --> 00:11:44,450
May I have a word?

195
00:11:44,700 --> 00:11:45,990
Of course, Donald.

196
00:11:46,870 --> 00:11:51,120
We've been getting reports of very angry behavior on your part.

197
00:11:51,460 --> 00:11:52,830
What?

198
00:11:51,460 --> 00:11:52,830
Threatening letters...

199
00:11:53,080 --> 00:11:54,960
...refusal to meet deadlines.

200
00:11:55,840 --> 00:11:58,800
Apparently people now call you Mental.

201
00:12:00,090 --> 00:12:01,420
Yeah.

202
00:12:03,180 --> 00:12:05,760
We want you to speak to a psychiatrist.

203
00:12:05,930 --> 00:12:07,850
Oh, no. Uh, you...

204
00:12:08,010 --> 00:12:10,520
You don't understand. This is so silly.

205
00:12:10,680 --> 00:12:14,350
Um, this is all just because of a sandwich.

206
00:12:15,480 --> 00:12:16,860
A sandwich?

207
00:12:17,310 --> 00:12:21,650
You see, my sister makes these amazing turkey sandwiches.

208
00:12:21,990 --> 00:12:26,950
Her secret is, she puts an extra slice of gravy-soaked bread in the middle.

209
00:12:27,200 --> 00:12:29,030
I call it "The Moistmaker."

210
00:12:30,040 --> 00:12:32,500
Anyway, I put my sandwich in the fridge...

211
00:12:32,660 --> 00:12:35,290
Ha-ha-ha. Oh, you know what?

212
00:12:35,540 --> 00:12:36,750
I'm sorry.

213
00:12:37,210 --> 00:12:38,920
I believe I ate that.

214
00:12:43,470 --> 00:12:44,880
You ate my sandwich?

215
00:12:45,430 --> 00:12:47,640
A simple mistake. It can happen to anyone.

216
00:12:47,890 --> 00:12:48,930
Oh, really?

217
00:12:51,390 --> 00:12:56,520
Did you confuse it with your own turkey sandwich with a Moistmaker?

218
00:12:57,400 --> 00:12:58,440
No, I...

219
00:12:58,650 --> 00:13:00,360
Do you, perhaps, remember...

220
00:13:00,570 --> 00:13:04,110
...seeing a note on top of it?

221
00:13:04,360 --> 00:13:08,450
There may have been a joke or limerick of some kind.

222
00:13:08,700 --> 00:13:10,530
That said it was...

223
00:13:10,740 --> 00:13:12,580
...my sandwich!

224
00:13:13,410 --> 00:13:14,910
Now calm down.

225
00:13:15,330 --> 00:13:18,250
Look in my office. Some may be in the trash.

226
00:13:20,340 --> 00:13:21,380
What?

227
00:13:22,670 --> 00:13:26,090
It was quite large. I had to throw most of it away.

228
00:13:28,090 --> 00:13:30,850
You threw my sandwich away?

229
00:13:31,970 --> 00:13:36,230
My sandwich?

230
00:13:38,440 --> 00:13:39,480
Hi.

231
00:13:38,440 --> 00:13:39,480
Hi.

232
00:13:39,770 --> 00:13:41,270
What's this book about?

233
00:13:41,520 --> 00:13:42,860
